  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 157 PM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nShower and storm activity will continue into the early with the \nremnants of Post Tropical Storm Vance from the Pacific bringing deep \nmoisture and left over vorticity into the region. Activity will wane \nfrom west to east through early afternoon hours as the disturbance \npushes east. The Weather Prediction Center has maintained portions \nof the Brush Country in a Marginal Risk (1 of 4) that extends into \nthe northeastern portions of the CWA. We have see isolated street \nflooding across the region with some of the stronger thunderstorms \ndue to the nature of the environment. We will dry out by Friday and \nconditions will persist through the weekend until our next front. \nOur next cold front is expected to swing through early next week in \nassociation with a potent low that will progress through the \nsouthern Great Plains. There is still some disagreements on a few \nthings such as timing and the extent of the associated front south. \nThough as it sits this will likely be our next chance for some \nactivity. Be sure check back for future updates. \n\nFor Halloween, around a 20% chance of showers will linger mainly in \nthe northeast of the Victoria Crossroads, though most locations will \nremain dry. Not only are we expected to be dry, but low temperatures \nwill stay in the 70s/upper 60s with light winds Halloween night. Our \npost Halloween crash will be warm and sunny through early next week. \n\nWill have to continue to monitor the possibility for minor coastal \nflooding along Gulf facing beaches into the weekend. This will be \ndue to persistent onshore flow and elevated swell periods. An \nincreased risk of rip currents will also persist.",
